<PropertyList include="f15-common-ex.xml">

    <sim>
        <description>Boeing F-15EX Eagle II</description>
        <long-description>
            The F-15EX Eagle II is the most modern version of the F-15 intoduced 52 years after the original F-15A model. The F-15EX is a
            high-performance, supersonic, allweather air-superiority fighter manufactured by St. Louis' Boing division powered by two
            F110-GE-129 turbofan engines. Unlike the original F-15C and F-15D, this aircraft has
            been designed to succeed in both air superiority and ground attack missions.
            Radar and heat seeking air-to-air missiles AIM-9X, AIM-120D and a 20mm gun are the primary armament.
            The Aircraft can carry and deploy MK-series bombs, CBU-series cluster bombs, GBU guided bombs, AGM missiles, and B61-7/12 nukes.
            Its raw power and acceleration but also targeting precision with the Sniper and LANTIRN targeting pods, along with the
            advanced LANTIRN Navigation Pod make it an unmatched fighter jet, along with its 104 kills to 0 losses ratio.
            MTOW ≈85,000 lbs. VNE ≈1,500 kts. Max Gear extension 300 kts. Max Flap speed 250 kts. Max dragchute speed 185 kts.
        </long-description>
        <variant-of>f15c</variant-of>
        <status>production</status>
